{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"86372cbd4b76439edb9041576abb7dfc01d63bf176d0f30946645635dc750c60","digest":{"component_or_area":"bridge CLI / mapping config","key_entities":["rebar bridge suggest-mapping","mapping_probe.py","mapping_config.py","bridge.py","_bridge_commands.py","_config_writer._emit_nested_toml","_config_writer._emit_config_toml","jira.JIRA.issue_types()","jira.JIRA.priorities()","jira.JIRA.issue_link_types()","jira.JIRA.statuses()","jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes()","jira.JIRA.search_issues()","jira.JIRA.transitions()","[tool.rebar.mapping]","projects.<KEY>"],"problem_keywords":["mapping configuration","jira probe","vocabulary discovery","toml serialization","read-only command"],"propositions":["Hand-authoring mapping vocabulary and axis maps is transcription-error-prone; a read-only probe command should query live Jira and emit suggested mapping configuration seeded with discovered project vocabulary and identity maps.","The new verb `rebar bridge suggest-mapping` must avoid collision with retired `bridge-probe` alias; it invokes a live Jira probe (via pycontribs) to observe issue types, statuses, priorities, link types, and hierarchy, then emits a TOML [tool.rebar.mapping] block.","Default invocation (no `--write`) serializes suggested mapping to stdout only; `--write` atomically merges into existing rebar.toml or creates one, preserving hand-edited flat [jira]/[tracker] sections and existing mapping keys via deep-merge.","Status vocabulary uses global Jira statuses (not per-project); transition hints are fetched from sample issues per type but flagged partial since Jira returns transitions only from current status; create_defaults stubs are emitted only for required createmeta fields not in the baseline create path.","TOML serialization requires an orchestrator that splits flat top-level config from nested [mapping.*] sub-tables, delegating each path to appropriate emitters while preserving _emit_toml's fail-closed contract on nesting.","Probe implementation reads only via documented pycontribs public API methods (no private REST); offline testing uses a fake port with canned discovery data, never live Jira credentials in CI."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787714334146190001,"uuid":"ff75bdff-e8c2-4d7c-bcc5-3ba0027676f4"}